      "math_academy_id": "e-4169",
      "problem": "Express $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=2}^{4} (2n-3)$ as a sum of three terms.",
      "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $2$ to $4.$ So, we compute the terms for $n=2,3,4$ and write the sum, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=2}^{4}(2n-3)&= \\overbrace{\\big(2(2)-3\\big)}^{\\large n\\,=\\,2}+\\overbrace{\\big(2(3)-3\\big)}^{\\large n\\,=\\,3}+\\overbrace{\\big(2(4)-3\\big)}^{\\large n\\,=\\,4} \\[-5pt]\n&=(4-3)+(6-3)+(8-3)\\[5pt]\n&=1+3+5\t\n\t}\n$$",
